WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.593
Hi, I'm Quoin!

00:00:02.593 --> 00:00:06.422
Here is how one terminal agent helps train the next one, twice over.

00:00:09.058 --> 00:00:13.359
The idea: turn your own verified successes into training data, refine with

00:00:13.359 --> 00:00:17.302
reinforcement learning, and let the improved model do the next round.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.405
The current model attempts terminal tasks under several harnesses.

00:00:22.405 --> 00:00:25.387
Each task's tests keep only the passing runs.

00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:29.116
It writes each success as a runbook, then solves the task again

00:00:29.116 --> 00:00:32.150
in a fresh sandbox, the runbook kept out of the log.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.738
Verified re-solves become fine-tuning data.

00:00:34.738 --> 00:00:36.906
Only the actor changes here.

00:00:37.326 --> 00:00:38.445
Then comes PPO.

00:00:38.445 --> 00:00:42.921
The inherited critic catches up alone for four updates, then both train

00:00:42.921 --> 00:00:44.413
on the verifier's reward.

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:48.135
The kept checkpoint becomes the next generation, and it does the

00:00:48.135 --> 00:00:49.335
next round of rewriting.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.774
Here is the formula.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.460
S is strict success: the whole test suite passed.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.320
Passed checks earn a bonus that never reaches one, so any

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.571
success outranks any failure.

00:01:02.192 --> 00:01:05.822
Run PPO straight from the base model, and a sparse test reward

00:01:05.822 --> 00:01:07.335
has nothing to push on.

00:01:07.755 --> 00:01:10.430
Rewrite first, and there are successes to reinforce.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:18.611
On Terminal-Bench two point one, the second rewrite stage reaches eighty-six point five two.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.887
The last PPO stage adds nothing.

00:01:22.258 --> 00:01:25.744
Over four suites, the first cycle adds about twenty-four points.

00:01:25.744 --> 00:01:27.138
The second, about six.

00:01:29.225 --> 00:01:32.109
The post calls it a new state of the art.

00:01:32.109 --> 00:01:35.570
On the paper's own chart, five models score higher on Terminal-Bench four.

00:01:36.725 --> 00:01:40.935
Rewriting manufactures the first successes that RL needs; the second cycle added

00:01:40.935 --> 00:01:43.040
about a quarter of the first.

00:01:44.858 --> 00:01:49.360
To recap: rewrite verified successes, refine with an inherited critic, and let

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.236
the new model rewrite next.

00:01:51.656 --> 00:01:53.739
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:53.739 --> 00:01:54.334
I'm Quoin.

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:54.632
Bye!
